  "query_preview": "..High pressure will remain in a favorable location to\ncontinue the ongoing monsoon surge through at least the next seven\ndays across the Beehive State. First though, all remaining heat\nheadlines were allowed to expire earlier this evening. \n\nAnother round of showers and thunderstorms with the threat of\nheavy rainfall will develop Monday afternoon across much of the\nregion. Again, like previous days, the most flood prone locations\nwill continue to be slot canyons, normally dry washes, slick rock\nareas as well as recent burn scars.\n\nLooking ahead, the Weather Prediction Center has Utah outlooked in\na marginal risk for flash flooding through the next 5 days...and\nguidance suggests this monsoon surge should continue into at \nleast next weekend if not early next week.",
